## 📂 Repository structure

```text
.
├── .streamlit/
│   └── config.toml                    # Streamlit theme + server config
├── data/                              # Raw Olist CSVs (not committed if >100 MB)
│   ├── olist_customers_dataset.csv
│   ├── olist_order_items_dataset.csv
│   ├── olist_order_reviews_dataset.csv
│   ├── olist_orders_dataset.csv
│   └── brazil-states.geojson          # optional — map falls back to remote mirror
├── docs/
│   ├── Customer satisfaction report.pdf
│   └── Customer-Satisfaction-Presentation.pptx
├── notebooks/
│   └── Data_cleaning.ipynb            # Data preparation & exploratory work
├── olist_app.py                       # Main Streamlit application
├── pora_logo.png                      # Branding asset (falls back to inline SVG)
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
└── LICENSE                            # MIT
```

> **`olist_dashboard.db`** — *if the SQLite file is present, document its
> purpose here* (e.g., "pre-joined analytical view consumed by the app").
> If the app reads CSVs directly, remove the file from the repo.

