## 🧪 Quality checks (verified before Cloud deploy)

- ✅ No `hash()` in Streamlit widget keys (deterministic keys only)
- ✅ No `st.session_state` writes to widget-owned keys
- ✅ Every cached function includes the file-signature in its key
- ✅ Matplotlib `Agg` backend + `runner.fixMatplotlib = true`
- ✅ All figures closed after render (no matplotlib memory leak)
- ✅ `pd.cut(..., right=False)` — FutureWarning-free on pandas 2.x
- ✅ Empty-state styling has no double border
- ✅ `prefers-reduced-motion`, `:focus-visible`, mobile breakpoints at 1100 px & 768 px
- ✅ Webfont fallback (`Inter` → system sans) so first paint is never blank
- ✅ Graceful degradation when GeoJSON fetch fails

---

## 📚 Data

The dataset is the public **Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist**
on Kaggle:
<https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/olistbr/brazilian-ecommerce>.

Four of the nine CSVs are used:

| Table | Rows | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| `olist_orders_dataset.csv` | 99,441 | Order timeline, delivery dates, status |
| `olist_customers_dataset.csv` | 99,441 | Customer geography, unique IDs |
| `olist_order_reviews_dataset.csv` | 99,224 | Review scores |
| `olist_order_items_dataset.csv` | 112,650 | Item prices, freight (GMV) |

The remaining five tables (payments, sellers, products, category translation,
geolocation) are intentionally excluded — see limitation **L4**.

